+in+the+self+scale+and+the+structure+of+interpersonal+closeness&#x00026;journal=J.+Pers.+Soc.+Psychol.&#x00026;volume=63&#x00026;pages=596-612\" target=\"_blank\">Google Scholar\u003C/a>\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"References\">\n\u003Cp class=\"ReferencesCopy1\">\u003Ca name=\"B9\" id=\"B9\">\u003C/a> Ashford, S. J. (1986). Feedback-seeking in individual adaptation: a resource perspective. \u003Ci>Acad. Manag. J.\u003C/i> 29, 465&#x02013;487. doi: 10.2307/256219\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp class=\"ReferencesCopy2\">\u003Ca href=\"https://doi.org/10.2307/256219\" target=\"_blank\">Crossref Full Text\u003C/a> | \u003Ca href=\"http://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?author=S.+J.+Ashford+&#x00026;publication_year=1986&#x00026;title=Feedback-seeking+in+individual+adaptation%3A+a+resource+perspective&#x00026;journal=Acad.+Manag.+J.&#x00026;volume=29&#x00026;pages=465-487\" target=\"_blank\">Google Scholar\u003C/a>\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"References\">\n\u003Cp class=\"ReferencesCopy1\">\u003Ca name=\"B10\" id=\"B10\">\u003C/a> Avolio, B. J., Sosik, J. J., Kahai, S. S., and Baker, B. (2014). E-leadership: re-examining transformations in leadership source and transmission. \u003Ci>Leadersh. Q.\u003C/i> 25, 105&#x02013;131. doi: 10.1016/j.leaqua.2013.11.003\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp class=\"ReferencesCopy2\">\u003Ca href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.leaqua.2013.11.003\" target=\"_blank\">Crossref Full Text\u003C/a> | \u003Ca href=\"http://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?author=B.+J.+Avolio&#x00026;author=J.+J.+Sosik&#x00026;author=S.+S.+Kahai&#x00026;author=B.+Baker+&#x00026;publication_year=2014&#x00026;title=E-leadership%3A+re-examining+transformations+in+leadership+source+and+transmission&#x00026;journal=Leadersh.+Q.&#x00026;volume=25&#x00026;pages=105-131\" target=\"_blank\">Google Scholar\u003C/a>\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"References\">\n\u003Cp class=\"ReferencesCopy1\">\u003Ca name=\"B11\" id=\"B11\">\u003C/a> Bar-Anan, Y., Liberman, N., and Trope, Y. (2006). The association between psychological distance and construal level: evidence from an implicit association test. \u003Ci>J. Exp. Psychol.\u003C/i> 135, 609&#x02013;622. doi: 10.1037/0096-3445.135.4.609\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp class=\"ReferencesCopy2\">\u003Ca href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17087576\" target=\"_blank\">PubMed Abstract\u003C/a> | \u003Ca href=\"https://doi.org/10.1037/0096-3445.135.4.609\" target=\"_blank\">Crossref Full Text\u003C/a> | \u003Ca href=\"http://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?author=Y.+Bar-Anan&#x00026;author=N.+Liberman&#x00026;author=Y.+Trope+&#x00026;publication_year=2006&#x00026;title=The+association+between+psychological+distance+and+construal+level%3A+evidence+from+an+implicit+association+test&#x00026;journal=J.+Exp.+Psychol.&#x00026;volume=135&#x00026;pages=609-622\" target=\"_blank\">Google Scholar\u003C/a>\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"References\">\n\u003Cp class=\"ReferencesCopy1\">\u003Ca name=\"B12\" id=\"B12\">\u003C/a> Belding, J. N., Naufel, K. Z., and Fujita, K. (2015). Using high-level construal and perceptions of changeability to promote self-change over self-protection motives in response to negative feedback. \u003Ci>Pers. Soc. Psychol. Bull.\u003C/i> 41, 822&#x02013;838. doi: 10.1177/0146167215580776\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp class=\"ReferencesCopy2\">\u003Ca href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25910942\" target=\"_blank\">PubMed Abstract\u003C/a> | \u003Ca href=\"https://doi.org/10.1177/0146167215580776\" target=\"_blank\">Crossref Full Text\u003C/a> | \u003Ca href=\"http://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?author=J.+N.+Belding&#x00026;author=K.+Z.+Naufel&#x00026;author=K.+Fujita+&#x00026;publication_year=2015&#x00026;title=Using+high-level+construal+and+perceptions+of+changeability+to+promote+self-change+over+self-protection+motives+in+response+to+negative+feedback&#x00026;journal=Pers.+Soc.+Psychol.+Bull.&#x00026;volume=41&#x00026;pages=822-838\" target=\"_blank\">Google Scholar\u003C/a>\u0